{"kind": "text", "at": "2026-08-02T14:48:40.891945+00:00", "text": "## Progress

- Added direct `CurveProjectivity` imports to [FGAPicRepresentability.lean](/home/axel/LeanAlgebraicGeometry-Horizon/MainProjects/Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge/AlgebraicJacobian/Picard/FGAPicRepresentability.lean:11) and [Pic0AbelianVariety.lean](/home/axel/LeanAlgebraicGeometry-Horizon/MainProjects/Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge/AlgebraicJacobian/Picard/Pic0AbelianVariety.lean:14). Consumer-only probes resolve `Adelic.isProjective_of_smoothProperGeometricallyIntegral`.
- Broke the resulting import cycle by extracting [HasRationalPoint.lean](/home/axel/LeanAlgebraicGeometry-Horizon/MainProjects/Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge/AlgebraicJacobian/Picard/HasRationalPoint.lean:31). Direct FGA and Pic0 compilation is green apart from existing sorry warnings.
- Added reusable coproduct infrastructure in [QuasiProjectiveFiniteInAffine.lean](/home/axel/LeanAlgebraicGeometry-Horizon/MainProjects/Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge/AlgebraicJacobian/Picard/QuasiProjectiveFiniteInAffine.lean:758). Projective or `IsProjectiveWith` pieces now assemble into `FiniteInAffine`, and the canonical `Over S` coproduct obtains `LocallyOfFiniteType ∧ FiniteInAffine`.
- All new declarations report only `propext`, `Classical.choice`, and `Quot.sound`. Narrow module builds passed. No umbrella build was needed because the umbrella was untouched.
- Main commits: `a2019afe66`, `77585ea619`, `d42d44fc28`, `bdff30e2aa`, graph commits `b2db9fd9f1`/`c8c4273ea1`, and state commit `61ed8d8bd4`.
- Restored 174 generated timestamp-only hgraph changes after independent audit. Current AJC hgraph residual is zero.

## Issues

- No intrinsic Picard degree carrier, arbitrary-field PicEt producer, representing `Pic^d` schemes, or projectivity/very-ampleness theorem for the actual Picard pieces landed.
- The central `fgaPicardRepresentability` sorry is unchanged, and no new `(rep :)` consumer was added.
- Fresh shared-index measurement at `959440af34`: lock present; 24,676 staged paths, 11,399 insertions and 421,909 deletions. All 43 task-authored/checked disk paths match `HEAD`, and every task commit remains an ancestor.

## Why I Stopped

The next honest step requires an intrinsic degree morphism from the étale Picard sheaf to the constant étale sheaf `ℤ`, then genuine degree fibres and their projectivity. A generic Abel-image range wrapper did not establish that mathematics, so it was removed before commit. The task remains queued and the roadmap row remains pending.

## Next

Construct the étale degree morphism and `Pic^d` fibre functors, represent those fibres, prove their `IsProjectiveWith` witnesses, then feed them into the new canonical coproduct theorem for `PointedPicSharpRep`.", "tool": "", "data": {}, "usage": null}
